{
 "about": "Marks on printed parts' edges, in pixels of 1920x1080 frames of the Prusa CORE One's camera as it stood for the 2026-10-10 print of petg-printer-reset-nozzle-on-part, from that print's own operator frames. Each curve's points lie on the planned outline `what` names at height `z` (`top`: that layer's outer walls, here the silver outer faces' top edges; `first`: every first-layer extrusion, here the parts' edges against the sheet), and `zc_mm` is the height the print had reached when the frame was taken, read off the slice at the frame's recorded progress. Each point was placed on a part's edge and moved to the strongest brightness edge within a few pixels of it, and only points whose crop shows them on that edge are kept. The landmarks are chassis features that hold within a pixel across every operator frame of the print.",
